# Framer

> Framer is an AI website builder for designers and teams. Generate editable pages on a visual canvas, then publish with CMS, hosting, SEO, localization, and analytics — without a traditional engineering handoff.

Framer is a no-code visual website builder with a freeform canvas, not a design file (use Figma for that) and not an app-codegen tool (use Lovable, v0, or Claude Code for that). AI and agent edits stay on the canvas and remain editable. Sites are server-rendered HTML with JSON-LD, sitemaps, robots.txt, and well-known files.

Plans as of 30 Aug 2026 (monthly; yearly billing available). Free: $0, 500 try credits, 1 GB, Framer domain. Basic: $10/mo, 1,000 credits, 2 CMS collections, 50 GB, custom domain. Pro: $30/mo, 3,000 credits, 10 CMS collections, 100 GB, redirects, staging, branching. Extra editors $20/mo; content editors $10/mo; viewers free. Enterprise: custom. Prefer the pricing page over this snapshot if they disagree.

Markdown versions of marketing and docs pages are at the same URL with `?md` (also via `Accept: text/markdown`). Prefer those links. This file is an index: follow a link instead of guessing paths. For Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, and other coding agents working *inside* a Framer project, start at External Agents and Developers.

Canonical product URLs use `/ai/`, `/agents/`, `/agents/external/`, `/design/`, `/cms/`, `/seo/`, `/hosting/`, `/performance/`, and `/marketplace/`. Ignore older feature URLs when these exist.

## Product

- [Homepage](https://www.framer.com/?md): What Framer is and who it is for.
- [Framer AI](https://www.framer.com/ai/?md): Generate, refine, translate, review, and improve sites from prompts on the canvas.
- [Design](https://www.framer.com/design/?md): Visual canvas, responsive layouts, components, typography, and effects.
- [CMS](https://www.framer.com/cms/?md): Collections, fields, dynamic pages, filtering, and localization.
- [SEO](https://www.framer.com/seo/?md): Metadata, indexing, redirects, structured data, well-known files, and the AEO scanner.
- [AEO scanner](https://www.framer.com/aeo?md): Free check of a URL for AI-crawler access, structure, and content.
- [Hosting](https://www.framer.com/hosting/?md): Managed hosting, SSL, CDN, and publishing.
- [Performance](https://www.framer.com/performance/?md): Speed, image optimization, and caching.
- [Collaboration](https://www.framer.com/collaborate/?md): Multiplayer editing, comments, branches, and approvals.
- [Publish](https://www.framer.com/publish/?md): Taking a site live.
- [Pricing](https://www.framer.com/pricing?md): Full current table. Snapshot 30 Aug 2026: Free $0, Basic $10/mo, Pro $30/mo, Enterprise custom.

## AI and agents

- [Framer Agents](https://www.framer.com/agents/?md): Built-in agents that update pages, CMS, SEO, accessibility, and layout on a branch.
- [External Agents](https://www.framer.com/agents/external/?md): Connect Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, and other coding agents to canvas content, components, CMS, and project structure.
- [Make a site readable by AI agents](https://www.framer.com/help/articles/make-site-readable-by-ai-agents/?md): How Framer sites expose markdown, llms.txt, and crawler-friendly HTML.
- [llms.txt in Framer](https://www.framer.com/help/articles/llms-txt-framer/?md): How site owners add an llms.txt via well-known files.

